 html=reviewhead(f'Direction {key.upper()} — {d["name"]}',1)+f'<main class="review-main"><p class="overline">DIRECTION {key.upper()} / EXPLORATION ONLY</p><h1>{d["name"]}</h1><p class="lead">{d["core"]}</p><div class="gate">No winner selected. All logo, palette and typography choices are exploratory. Owner outcomes: A / B / C / REJECT / HYBRID.</div><a href="{folder}-overview.png"><img class="overview" src="{folder}-overview.png" alt="Direction {key.upper()} overview board: logos, palette, patient, doctor and mobile examples"></a><section><h2>Concept sheet</h2>{sheet}</section><section id="logos"><h2>Two independent logo ideas</h2>{concepts}<p>No trademark search or legal clearance claimed. Both marks remain unselected. A1/B1/C1 in screen headers are placement specimens only.</p></section><section><h2>Exploratory color system</h2><p class="overline">EXPLORATORY — NOT FINAL BRAND PALETTE</p>{swatches(d)}<p>Identity, surface, text, accent and functional status roles are separate. All statuses carry text; color alone conveys no consequence.</p></section>{typeproof}<nav class="screen-links" aria-label="Screen examples">'+''.join(f'<a href="#{kind}">{label}</a>' for kind,label in SCREEN_LABELS)+f'</nav>{examples}<section class="gate"><h2>Owner decision required</h2><p>A / B / C / REJECT / HYBRID</p><p>A hybrid must name the elements to combine and be rendered coherently for later approval. Selection does not create Final Brand V2.</p></section></main></body></html>'
